<main class="pt-[100px] pb-20"><div class="mx-auto max-w-[1000px] px-6">
  <nav class="mb-6 text-sm text-white/40"><a href="/" class="hover:text-white">Home</a><span class="mx-2">&#8250;</span><span class="text-white/60">Adoption Trends</span></nav>

  <h1 class="font-display text-[clamp(28px,4vw,40px)] font-bold tracking-tight mb-4">Technology Adoption Trends</h1>
  <div class="rounded-xl border border-accent/20 bg-accent/[0.05] p-5 mb-8">
    <p class="text-[15px] text-white/80">
      What businesses <span class="text-emerald-400 font-semibold">installed</span> and
      <span class="text-red-400 font-semibold">dropped</span> in the last 30 days, counted from
      observed tech-stack changes across millions of continuously re-crawled live websites.
      Not survey data, not npm downloads: production deployments.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="rounded-[20px] border border-white/[0.07] bg-[#111B33] overflow-hidden mb-10">
    <div class="overflow-x-auto"><table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse min-w-[500px]">
      <thead><tr>
        <th class="px-5 py-2.5 text-left text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-white/35 font-semibold border-b border-white/[0.07]">Technology</th>
        <th class="px-5 py-2.5 text-right text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-white/35 font-semibold border-b border-white/[0.07]">Installed (30d)</th>
        <th class="px-5 py-2.5 text-right text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-white/35 font-semibold border-b border-white/[0.07]">Dropped (30d)</th>
        <th class="px-5 py-2.5 text-right text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-white/35 font-semibold border-b border-white/[0.07]">Net</th>
      </tr></thead>
      <tbody><%= for [tech, adds, drops] <- @movers do %>
        <tr class="hover:bg-white/[0.015]">
          <td class="px-5 py-3 border-b border-white/[0.07] text-white font-medium">
            <a href={"/trends/#{slugify(tech)}"} class="hover:text-accent"><%= tech %></a>
          </td>
          <td class="px-5 py-3 border-b border-white/[0.07] text-right text-emerald-400/90 tabular-nums"><%= format_number(adds) %></td>
          <td class="px-5 py-3 border-b border-white/[0.07] text-right text-red-400/80 tabular-nums"><%= format_number(drops) %></td>
          <td class="px-5 py-3 border-b border-white/[0.07] text-right"><.net_badge adds={adds} drops={drops} /></td>
        </tr>
      <% end %></tbody>
    </table></div>
  </div>

  <div class="rounded-xl border border-accent/20 bg-accent/5 p-6 mb-10 text-center">
    <p class="text-white/80 mb-3 font-medium">Every install above is a business that just changed its stack, the best moment to reach them.</p>
    <a href="/signup" data-umami-event="signup_cta" data-umami-event-source="trends_gate"
       class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-xl bg-accent px-7 py-3.5 font-display text-sm font-semibold text-white hover:bg-accent-hover hover:-translate-y-0.5 transition-all">
      Get this week's adopters as a list, emails included
    </a>
  </div>

  <section class="mb-10" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/FAQPage">
    <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold mb-4">How this is measured</h2>
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-white/[0.07] bg-white/[0.02] p-5" itemscope itemprop="mainEntity" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question">
      <h3 itemprop="name" class="font-medium text-white mb-2">Where do these numbers come from?</h3>
      <div itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
        <p itemprop="text" class="text-sm text-white/60">ListSignal continuously re-crawls millions of live business websites and diffs each site's detected technology stack between crawls. "Installed" means a technology appeared on a site where it wasn't before; "dropped" means it disappeared. Counts cover the trailing 30 days and update daily.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</div></main>
<footer class="border-t border-white/[0.07] py-8 text-center text-[13px] text-white/35">&copy; 2026 ListSignal</footer>